{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 18:19:31.797641", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Description\\nThe network is an SDN star topology with one central switch (switch_0) and multiple edge switches (switch_1, switch_2, switch_3, switch_4). Hosts (host_1, host_2, host_3, host_4) are connected to edge switches, and all devices share a single access subnet (10.0.0.0/24). The SDN controller operates at 20.0.0.100 and manages the switches via OpenFlow.\\n\\n#### Reachability Analysis\\nThe reachability test results between hosts are as follows:\\n\\n1. **Host-to-Host Communication:**\\n   - **host_1 → host_2:** Status: Unknown (No data available for transmission or reception).\\n   - **host_1 → host_4:** Status: Unknown (No data available for transmission or reception).\\n   - **host_2 → host_4:** Status: OK (2 packets transmitted, 2 received, 0% loss, average RTT: 13.157 ms).\\n   - **host_3 → host_2:** Status: OK (2 packets transmitted, 2 received, 0% loss, average RTT: 14.345 ms).\\n   - **host_3 → host_4:** Status: OK (2 packets transmitted, 2 received, 0% loss, average RTT: 13.527 ms).\\n   - **host_4 → host_2:** Status: OK (2 packets transmitted, 2 received, 0% loss, average RTT: 13.01 ms).\\n\\n#### Observations\\n1. **Abnormal Behavior:**\\n   - Host_1 appears to have connectivity issues with host_2 and host_4. The status for these tests is \"unknown,\" indicating that no packets were transmitted or received, and no RTT data is available.\\n   - Other hosts (host_2, host_3, host_4) demonstrate normal communication with each other, with no packet loss and reasonable RTT values.\\n\\n2. **Localized Fault:**\\n   - The issue seems to be isolated to host_1 or its associated edge switch (switch_1). This is inferred from the lack of communication between host_1 and other hosts, while other hosts communicate successfully.\\n\\n3. **Potential Root Cause:**\\n   - The problem may stem from host_1\\'s network configuration, its connection to switch_1, or switch_1\\'s connectivity to the central switch (switch_0). Alternatively, there could be an issue with the OpenFlow rules or SDN controller configuration affecting host_1\\'s traffic.\\n\\n#### Next Steps\\nFurther investigation is required to pinpoint the root cause. This includes:\\n- Verifying host_1\\'s network configuration.\\n- Checking switch_1\\'s connectivity and OpenFlow rules.\\n- Ensuring the SDN controller is correctly managing switch_1 and host_1\\'s traffic.\\n\\nThis concludes the initial diagnostic report., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='c28740f1-ab7d-4f71-b1f2-cf3573b6a805'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
